Operational Efficiency and Maintenance Remain Key Challenges

Semiconductor scrubber systems require ongoing maintenance and operational monitoring to maintain treatment effectiveness.

High equipment costs, facility-integration complexity and consumption of water, electricity and other consumables can influence purchasing decisions.

Facilities must also balance emissions-treatment performance with equipment uptime and maintenance requirements.

Because exhaust-treatment interruptions can affect connected semiconductor manufacturing equipment, qualification and operational reliability are particularly important.

